        null
    ],
    "optionsVersion": 1,
    "apiVersion": "VERSION_0",
    "isResourceIntensiveScript": false,
    "showPartitioning": false,
    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Validates data against a rules table or typed rules (not empty, unique, ranges, lists, patterns, emails, postcodes, field comparisons) with violations per row and per rule.",
    "category": "Preparation",
    "subcategory": "Data quality",
    "tags": [
        "data validation",
        "data quality",
        "rules",
        "checks",
        "audit",
        "master data",
        "testing",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Checks data against a list of **validation rules** and reports every violation, a summary per rule and a pass / fail flag per row.\n\nRules come from a **rules table on input 2** (Field, Check, Value, Severity, optional Rule Name), so business users can maintain them, or are typed in the options one per line: `Field | CHECK | value | severity`.\n\n**Checks**: NOT_EMPTY, UNIQUE, MIN, MAX, BETWEEN (`low..high`), ALLOWED and NOT_ALLOWED (`a|b|c`), PATTERN (regular expression), MIN_LENGTH, MAX_LENGTH, IS_NUMBER, IS_DATE, NOT_FUTURE, EMAIL, UK_POSTCODE, COMPARE with another field (`<= Credit Limit`), REQUIRED_IF another field has a value (`Country = UK`).\n\n**Severity** is Error or Warning; a row is *Valid* when it has no errors. Empty values pass every check except NOT_EMPTY and REQUIRED_IF, so each problem is reported once.\n\nOutputs: one row per violation (with your key fields), one row per rule with failures, rate, status and examples, and the input with error and warning counts.",
    "dependencies": "",
